{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01424",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.05,
      "end_seconds": 6.54,
      "duration_seconds": 5.49,
      "text": "Doctor, I've brought them through. The observations are done, whenever you need them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.89,
      "end_seconds": 13.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.23,
      "text": "Thanks. Hello, come in, sit down. What brings you in today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 14.73,
      "end_seconds": 18.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor. I came along to help out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 19.94,
      "end_seconds": 28.97,
      "duration_seconds": 9.03,
      "text": "I've been dealing with bloating after meals. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.56,
      "end_seconds": 40.62,
      "duration_seconds": 6.06,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been? I'll explain everything as we go along."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.68,
      "end_seconds": 46.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Since yesterday, that's when it began."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.95,
      "end_seconds": 53.34,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.94,
      "end_seconds": 59.96,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "Severe, I'd say. I notice it more with large meals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.86,
      "end_seconds": 66.29,
      "duration_seconds": 5.43,
      "text": "I was just going to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 66.39,
      "end_seconds": 73.11,
      "duration_seconds": 6.72,
      "text": "Sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.05,
      "end_seconds": 76.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Later, thanks. Please go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.2,
      "end_seconds": 85.85,
      "duration_seconds": 7.65,
      "text": "Oh, and a lot of wind. That's been about the same, about a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.84,
      "end_seconds": 90.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Is it bearing on you a lot?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.34,
      "end_seconds": 101.18,
      "duration_seconds": 8.84,
      "text": "It's mild, honestly. Loose stools now and then was there, but it's gone away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 103.11,
      "end_seconds": 105.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Mm, that's what happened, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.74,
      "end_seconds": 115.22,
      "duration_seconds": 7.48,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any weight loss, blood in the stool or night-time diarrhoea?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.05,
      "end_seconds": 119.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "No, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.94,
      "end_seconds": 121.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "Nothing like vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.81,
      "end_seconds": 124.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Nope, no vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.5,
      "end_seconds": 129.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Is your chest okay generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.24,
      "end_seconds": 135.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.07,
      "text": "Breathing's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.42,
      "end_seconds": 140.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.94,
      "end_seconds": 148.76,
      "duration_seconds": 6.82,
      "text": "It's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a round yellow one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.44,
      "end_seconds": 152.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.11,
      "end_seconds": 169.89,
      "duration_seconds": 15.78,
      "text": "For the anxiety, I believe. My wife sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. Alendronate. I take it 70 milligrams, once a week for my bones."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 171.88,
      "end_seconds": 178.45,
      "duration_seconds": 6.57,
      "text": "That's what's prescribed, but I'm not sure she takes it every day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.26,
      "end_seconds": 187.74,
      "duration_seconds": 8.48,
      "text": "Tiotropium inhaler. I take it once a day for my chest. It's peppermint capsules, after meals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.94,
      "end_seconds": 195.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "Okay, what conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.82,
      "end_seconds": 200.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Um, I've had anxiety, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.4,
      "end_seconds": 202.15,
      "duration_seconds": 0.75,
      "text": "Mm-hmm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.12,
      "end_seconds": 209.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "I've got thin bones. I've had COPD for two years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.52,
      "end_seconds": 212.22,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.6,
      "end_seconds": 227.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.23,
      "end_seconds": 231.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "I'll have a glass of wine with dinner."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.17,
      "end_seconds": 234.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "How about smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.05,
      "end_seconds": 238.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "I gave up cigarettes last spring."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.75,
      "end_seconds": 242.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "So, do you follow any particular diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 243.83,
      "end_seconds": 247.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "I'm vegetarian and have been for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.18,
      "end_seconds": 253.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "Alright, are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.59,
      "end_seconds": 264.78,
      "duration_seconds": 10.19,
      "text": "I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.83,
      "end_seconds": 269.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "Did you ever have any procedures done?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 270.72,
      "end_seconds": 275.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "Yes, I had a bunion operation, six years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 291.49,
      "end_seconds": 303.33,
      "duration_seconds": 11.84,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Pulse is 69 beats a minute, temperature is 36.5 degrees. BP is 118 over 77, oxygen saturation is 97 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.15,
      "end_seconds": 306.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.69,
      "end_seconds": 311.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Right, let's have a proper look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.28,
      "end_seconds": 315.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Hold that for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.68,
      "end_seconds": 330.14,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "Your tummy is soft and not tender, and I can't feel any lumps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.87,
      "end_seconds": 358.72,
      "duration_seconds": 24.85,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again. Okay, so my impression is this: This is probably a functional bowel pattern, with no alarm features. Irritable bowel syndrome is also on my list. A coeliac blood test is what I'd like next, for bloating. Try smaller meals and keep a food and symptom diary for four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 359.81,
      "end_seconds": 371.71,
      "duration_seconds": 11.9,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if you see blood in the stool or lose weight, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 373.3,
      "end_seconds": 375.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "That's fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 376.36,
      "end_seconds": 381.71,
      "duration_seconds": 5.35,
      "text": "Come back in six weeks. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 383.46,
      "end_seconds": 388.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "Ah, okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    }
  ]
}